<!--
    GH-1243: 8051 16-bit ADD not identified. The 8051 ADDC SLEIGH semantics
    computed the carry-in add in a 1-byte temp (tmp:1 = $(CY) + op), which
    truncates the carry-out when (op + carry_in) overflows a byte
    (e.g. 0xff + 1 = 0x100 -> 0x00). The CY flag is then set wrong and
    ADD+ADDC multi-byte (16/32-bit) add chains are not recognised.

    Fix (kuna GH-1243): a do_addc(op) macro performs the add in a 2-byte temp
    so the carry-out survives, then sets CY from the full result and stores the
    low byte into ACC.

    Behavioural discriminator (bytes below):
      0x0000 SETB CY        CY = 1
      0x000e MOV  A,#0x0    A  = 0
      0x0010 ADDC A,#0xff   FIXED: 0 + 0xff + 1 = 0x100 -> A=0, CY=1
                            BUGGY: tmp:1 = 1 + 0xff = 0x00 -> A=0, CY=0
      0x0012 MOV  A,#0x0
      0x0014 JNC  0x18      FIXED: CY=1, no jump  BUGGY: CY=0, jumps
      0x0016 MOV  A,#0x2
      0x0018 MOV  P1,A      FIXED: P1 = 2         BUGGY: P1 = 0

    The earlier ADDC at 0x0003 (0xff + 0 + 1) overflows ACC directly and is
    correct in both forms, so P0 = 1 either way; it guards against the fix
    breaking the already-correct case. Stage: pcode lift (SLEIGH spec-fix).
-->
